enforcement|making-rules-observed|NOUN|action ensuring rules are followed|Action taken to make sure that a law, rule, or agreement is obeyed.|sự thực thi; việc bảo đảm tuân thủ|The council discussed the enforcement of parking restrictions.|Hội đồng thảo luận việc thực thi các quy định hạn chế đỗ xe.|Uncountable; enforcement of names the rule or obligation being upheld.|0
imaginary|not-real|ADJECTIVE|existing in imagination|Existing only in someone's imagination rather than in the real world.|tưởng tượng; không có thật|The child drew a map of an imaginary island.|Đứa trẻ vẽ bản đồ một hòn đảo tưởng tượng.|Used before a noun or after a linking verb; imaginary differs from imaginative, which describes creativity.|0
primate|animal-group|NOUN|member of the primate group|A mammal belonging to the biological group that includes monkeys, apes, and humans.|động vật linh trưởng|The museum display compares the hands of several primates.|Khu trưng bày của bảo tàng so sánh bàn tay của một số loài linh trưởng.|Countable in this animal sense; plural primates. The religious title primate is a different sense.|-
surprised|unexpected-feeling|ADJECTIVE|feeling something was unexpected|Feeling that something is unexpected or different from what you thought would happen.|ngạc nhiên|I was surprised to find the library open so early.|Tôi ngạc nhiên khi thấy thư viện mở cửa sớm như vậy.|Surprised at or by something, surprised to do something, and surprised that introduce the cause.|0
waste|discarded-material|NOUN|material that is no longer wanted|Material left over or thrown away because it is no longer wanted or useful.|chất thải; vật liệu bỏ đi|The workshop separates metal waste from paper and plastic.|Xưởng tách phế liệu kim loại khỏi giấy và nhựa.|Usually uncountable for discarded material; waste from a process identifies its source.|0
waste|poor-use|NOUN|unnecessary loss of a resource|The unnecessary use or loss of something valuable, such as time, money, or materials.|sự lãng phí|Printing the same document twice was a waste of paper.|In cùng một tài liệu hai lần là sự lãng phí giấy.|A waste of names the resource used without a useful result.|1
waste|use-badly|VERB|use a resource without enough benefit|To use time, money, or another resource without getting enough value or benefit from it.|lãng phí|We wasted an hour looking for a file in the wrong folder.|Chúng tôi lãng phí một giờ tìm một tệp trong nhầm thư mục.|Transitive waste something; waste time doing something takes an ing form.|2
waste|discarded|ADJECTIVE|left over and unwanted|Left over from use or a process and no longer wanted.|phế thải; thừa bỏ đi|Waste wood from the factory is collected in a separate container.|Gỗ phế thải từ nhà máy được thu gom trong một thùng riêng.|Usually before a material noun, as in waste paper or waste water; not the verb construction.|3
